WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.036
-Thank you so much for tuning in
and watching "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.737
I'm Jimmy Fallon.
I really appreciate this.

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.606
It makes me happy.
I'm happy to be here.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.142
Let's get to the news
and some jokes here.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:12.611
Well, guys, I hope everyone had
a nice Labor Day weekend.

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:15.414
It was actually a busy
Labor Day for President Trump.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:17.683
He held a 45-minute press
conference where he launched

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:20.586
an attack against leaders
of the U.S. military.

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.122
He launched more
insults at Joe Biden.

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:25.858
And he even launched something
from his nose.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:29.695
[ Slow-mo rumbling noise ]

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:31.630
Pshew!
[ Audience ohs ]

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.800
Ooh-ee! Oh! What was that?
Eww!

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.269
Eww!

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.471
People are wondering, man.
Was that a booger?

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:40.173
Was it drugs?

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.674
I'd like to think he was
eating crackers

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.743
by sticking them up his nose.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:46.045
Hey, you know what could have
stopped that projectile?

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.581
A mask.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.916
Even worse, whatever
flew out of his nose

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:53.119
hit that U.S. Open
line judge in the throat.

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.955
And that's --
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.590
You don't like to see that.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.992
Well, everyone is still talking
about "The Atlantic's" report

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:03.796
that Trump called fallen service
members "losers" and "suckers."

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.498
And yesterday, when Trump
was asked about it,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.300
he once again denied
ever saying it.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.568
Listen to his response.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.969
-Who would say a thing
like that?

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:12.005
Only an animal would say
a thing like that.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.207
-Yeah. I bet if an animal
did say that,

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.008
it would probably be this one.

00:01:16.008 --> 00:01:17.343
I don't want to -- I don't --
Look --

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.878
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:21.848
Other than the 245 times Trump
has actually called someone

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:23.883
a loser and a sucker
on Twitter,

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.352
he'd never say
anything like that.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.520
That's right. Trump allegedly
made outrageously

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.291
offensive remarks,
so you know what that means.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.060
Nothing happens to Trump,
and Billy Bush gets fired.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.896
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.364
I'm not sure what's
more upsetting,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.933
the comments Trump
reportedly made,

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.334
or what he's going to do
to change the subject.

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:44.871
[ As Trump ] "And that's why
we're nuking the moon."

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.806
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.774
That was a pretty crazy
press conference.

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:50.243
At one point, Trump went off
on a rant

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.278
attacking military leaders.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.914
Because when you're in a scandal
about calling soldiers names,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:58.384
the best defense is to
antagonize their bosses.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:01.120
Trump was like, "And this goes
all the way to the top, people,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.956
whoever is the chief
of all the commanders."

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:07.426
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.262
If that wasn't enough,
at that same press conference,

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:12.432
Trump told a reporter
to take off his mask.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.666
Watch this.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.268
-The issue of what happened

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.203
when you were in France
continues to be a story.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:18.704
-You're going to have to
take that off, please.

00:02:18.704 --> 00:02:20.206
Just -- you can take it off.
You're --

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.508
How many feet are you away?
-I'll speak a lot louder.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.778
-Well, if you don't take it
off, you're very muffled.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:28.113
So if you would take it off,
it would be a lot easier.

00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:29.949
-I'll just speak a lot louder.
Is that better?

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.085
-[ Huffs ]
It's better, yeah.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.653
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.653 --> 00:02:35.888
-What is Trump doing?

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:37.656
He's the president
of the United States,

00:02:37.656 --> 00:02:40.026
not Velma at the end of
an episode of "Scooby Doo."

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.494
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:42.562
[ Gasps ]

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.330
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.732
Meanwhile, it looks like all the
scandals that have plagued

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:48.234
Trump's presidency are starting
to catch up with him.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.402
Check it out.

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:50.837 line:0%
-The president is disputing

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.571 line:0%
a report in "The New York Times"

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.908 line:0%
that his campaign has squandered
its fund-raising advantage.

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:59.846
-They burned through
$800 million of the $1.1 billion

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.480
they raised since 2019,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.516
some of what are described
as vanity splurges.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.018
-Yeah. You could tell
he's strapped for cash

00:03:06.018 --> 00:03:08.454
because now all his speeches
have product placements.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:12.058
"We'll repeal Obamacare
and replace it with...

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.727
delicious, nutritious
Boar's Head --

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:18.097
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:20.400
Boar's Head cold cuts."

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.370
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.671
I don't know what
I'm holding there.

00:03:25.671 --> 00:03:28.040
Like a jar of cold cuts?

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.176
-A ham.
-A ham. That was good.

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.078
Give up the ham.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.580
Trump's campaign has already
spent $800 million,

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:37.283
and he's still losing
by almost ten points.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:39.051
So far,
it's the worst money spent

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.287
since you bought
Skechers Shape Ups.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:43.589
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:46.459
I'm working out.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:49.695
I'm going to the bar.
I'm feeling good, man.

00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:52.065
I gained a few,
but maybe it's muscle.

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:58.437
Seriously, they blew through
$800 million in a few months.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:01.407
Who's running his campaign?
Trump in the '80s?

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.109
[ Light laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:05.277
-In the '90s?

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.046
Now Trump's claiming
he's going to spend

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:09.849
up to $100 million
of his own money.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:11.083
It's a great idea.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:12.551
Mike Bloomberg heard
and was like,

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:15.087
"Yeah, good luck with that."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.087 --> 00:04:17.223
But the Trump campaign isn't
worried, especially because

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.657
they're about to bring in
a few million

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:20.893
from Don Jr.'s
Visine endorsement.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:24.297
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.033
The campaign also just spent

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:31.537
$156,000 on planes
that pull banners.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.673
So their advertising strategy
is basically the same

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:36.943
as the Clam Shack down
at the Jersey Shore.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.244
You can tell Trump's campaign is
running out of money

00:04:39.244 --> 00:04:40.980
because this weekend
they sunk a bunch of boats

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.315
for the insurance money.

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:46.452
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.220
Oh, my goodness.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.989
But this morning,
Trump denied the report

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:53.091
and sent a tweet saying that
they have lots of money.

00:04:53.091 --> 00:04:55.427
It would have been more
convincing if Trump's next tweet

00:04:55.427 --> 00:04:59.398
wasn't his Venmo handle
and the prayer hands emoji.

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:02.201
Could we see the last line
of his tweet again?

00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:05.237
Trump's tweets look like a spam
e-mail you shouldn't open.

00:05:05.237 --> 00:05:08.207
It's like, lots of dollar signs
and energy.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.242
Oh, that sounds --

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:12.478
Meanwhile, just when it seemed
like things couldn't sink

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.146
any lower for Trump
and his supporters,

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:15.915
it appears that they
literally can.

00:05:15.915 --> 00:05:16.949
Watch this.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.418 line:0%
-There were several boats

00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:21.353 line:0%
that sank during a lake parade
supporting President Trump.

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.589 line:0%
The sheriff's office says calls
started coming in almost

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.991 line:0%
immediately after the parade
started on Saturday.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:28.260 line:0%
At least three of the boats were
recovered,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.263 line:0%
but some are still
underwater.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.797
-You know if Trump
were on board,

00:05:31.797 --> 00:05:33.599
he would have been like, "Out of
the way, women and children.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:36.068
Presidents first.
Okay?

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:37.937
Thank you. Do you mind
if I step on your back

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.506
just to get out of here?
Thank you."

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:44.677
The event's Facebook page said,
"Let's really make a statement."

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.613
Unfortunately, that statement
was, "Help, my boat is sinking."

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.282
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:51.149
Ironically, while the boats
were sinking,

00:05:51.149 --> 00:05:53.085
Republicans in Congress
spent two months debating

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:56.655
whether or not to send them
a life raft.

00:05:56.655 --> 00:05:58.490
-Ah!

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:01.294
-Uh, that's your "New York
Times" joke of the week...

00:06:01.294 --> 00:06:04.196
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.196 --> 00:06:07.433
...sponsored by
Boar's Head cold cuts,

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:09.468
the finest jarred cold cuts.

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:11.870
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:14.307
Oh, man, this isn't good.
This weekend in California,

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:16.442
a wildfire started burning,

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.510
and it was caused by
a pretty unlikely source.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.179
This is real.
Listen to this.

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:23.182 line:0%
-The El Dorado fire here
in San Bernardino started by

00:06:23.182 --> 00:06:25.618 line:0%
a smoke-generating
pyrotechnic device

00:06:25.618 --> 00:06:27.820 line:0%
used at a gender reveal party.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.857
-Oh, my goodness.
They used pyrotechnics?

00:06:31.857 --> 00:06:34.193
Seriously.
It's a gender reveal,

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.995
not a KISS concert.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:42.368
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:52.311
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.980
Are you serious?

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:58.183
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.183 --> 00:06:59.551
Oh, man.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:01.653
Even people who fall off cliffs
taking selfies are like,

00:07:01.653 --> 00:07:03.055
"What a bunch of idiots."

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:04.957
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.957 --> 00:07:08.794
Yeah, it turns out the couple is
expecting six months in jail

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:10.896
and thousands of legal fees.

00:07:10.896 --> 00:07:13.165
And finally, listen to this.
The founder of Jelly Belly

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:14.767
announced that he is
going to give away

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.235
a Florida candy factory

00:07:16.235 --> 00:07:18.805
as part of a nationwide
treasure hunt.

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:21.474
It's great until you find out
it's the factory that makes

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:24.076
all the buttered popcorn
flavored jelly beans.

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:26.078
We have a great show for you
tonight.

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:28.180
The very funny Joel McHale
is here.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.448
[ Applause ]

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:33.853
His latest album "Detroit 2"
is number one on iTunes.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:35.955
We'll be talking to him,
and then he'll be performing

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:38.224
his latest single,
"Harder Than My Demons."

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:41.193
Big Sean is here.
[ Applause ]

00:07:41.193 --> 00:07:43.029
Love Big Sean.

00:07:43.029 --> 00:07:44.463
We're back after two weeks.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:45.931
Did you guys have a good break?

00:07:45.931 --> 00:07:49.335
-Um...yeah.
-Yeah.

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:51.504
-Wow. You didn't enjoy yourself?

00:07:51.504 --> 00:07:53.306
-It was okay.
-Yeah.

00:07:53.306 --> 00:07:56.375
What, just a lot of...
things happening?

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.478
-Yeah, you know.
Just chillin'.

00:07:58.478 --> 00:08:00.412
-Hmm.
-Hangin' out around the crib.

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:01.814
You know?
-What are you --

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:03.182
Are you watching
anything on TV?

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:04.750
What are you watching now
that's good?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.386
-Oh, man, what am I watching?

00:08:07.386 --> 00:08:09.555
You know, I've been watching
this thing

00:08:09.555 --> 00:08:12.090
called "Love Swindler."

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:15.093
[ Laughter ]
-Wait, what? What?

00:08:15.093 --> 00:08:17.129
-We -- we have different --
-It's crazy.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.464
It's like --
-Is it American?

00:08:18.464 --> 00:08:21.667
-Yeah, it's on Showtime.
It's about this dude who like --

00:08:21.667 --> 00:08:23.769
he swindled all these
unsuspecting

00:08:23.769 --> 00:08:27.139
middle-aged white women
out of their life savings.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:28.941
He just kept like
reinventing himself.

00:08:28.941 --> 00:08:32.377
He was like a plastic surgeon,
and then a real estate agent.

00:08:32.377 --> 00:08:35.080
Then he had, like,
this crab restaurant,

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.015
and he just -- you know,
he would go

00:08:37.015 --> 00:08:39.384
from town to town, like,
reinventing himself.

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:41.053
-Wait. "Love Swindler"?
-Yeah.

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:42.254
-And it's a documentary?

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:44.023
-It's a documentary series,
yeah.

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:45.524
-Oh, I want to check
that out.

00:08:45.524 --> 00:08:47.393
That's what I'm all about.
-It's on Showtime.

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:49.795
Yeah, you know, I'm about
the swindle life too.

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.396
-No, no, no, no, no.

00:08:51.396 --> 00:08:53.632
No, I'm into documentaries.
I'm into documentaries.

00:08:53.632 --> 00:08:55.234
-Yes.
-That's what I meant.

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:57.803
-Me too, yeah.
-I'm watching --

00:08:57.803 --> 00:08:59.304
I'm watching "The Vow."
Are you watching that?

00:08:59.304 --> 00:09:01.773
-Oh, yeah. Yeah.
-Whew!

00:09:01.773 --> 00:09:05.177
Dude, it's on HBO Max.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:06.379
-Yeah.

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:08.114
-I have like ten HBOs now.
-I know, right?

00:09:08.114 --> 00:09:09.448
-I had to sign up
for a whole new thing.

00:09:09.448 --> 00:09:11.550
-It's crazy.
-HBO Max. A whole new jam.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:13.085
-You can never find --
like, you know,

00:09:13.085 --> 00:09:14.720
if you don't watch something
in its entirety,

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.289
you can never get back
to the platform

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:18.724
that you were
watching it on.

00:09:18.724 --> 00:09:20.092
It's like,
"Wait, where did this thing --"

00:09:20.092 --> 00:09:21.860
-Yeah, where did I find that?
-Yeah.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.095
-Well, this, I found --

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:24.830
I read about it,
and then I found it,

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.499
and then I signed up,
and now I'm on that.

00:09:26.499 --> 00:09:28.266
But this thing
isn't a whole jam.

00:09:28.266 --> 00:09:30.735
You only get two -- it's only up
to like two or three --

00:09:30.735 --> 00:09:32.404
-Yeah, yeah. It's, you know,
a little bit at a time.

00:09:32.404 --> 00:09:33.705
I've been watching that too,
"The Vow."

00:09:33.705 --> 00:09:35.874
-It's fantastic.
You see it, Quest?

00:09:35.874 --> 00:09:38.510
-I have not seen it, no.
-Dude, it is nuts.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.312
Real deal, real deal
craziness.

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:41.714
It's wild.
I watched that.

00:09:41.714 --> 00:09:44.750
I watched "Class Action Park"
on HBO Max --

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.487
I feel like --
Boar's Head cold --

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:50.956
The NBC --

00:09:50.956 --> 00:09:53.225
But, no,
"Class Action Park,"

00:09:53.225 --> 00:09:54.760
have you seen that?
-No.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.994
-Have you seen that,
you guys?

00:09:55.994 --> 00:09:58.064
It's a real thing.
Anyone here seen that?

00:09:58.064 --> 00:10:00.499
It's -- Gerard, yeah.
Yeah, we went to it.

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:01.701
In my high school, I went to --

00:10:01.701 --> 00:10:03.869
Action Park was a theme park
in New Jersey.

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:05.438
But it basically has no rules.

00:10:05.438 --> 00:10:07.372
It's like -- and people were
just getting hurt

00:10:07.372 --> 00:10:08.574
every single --

00:10:08.574 --> 00:10:10.108
There was, like,
an alpine slide

00:10:10.108 --> 00:10:12.411
where you would just --
it was a plastic thing

00:10:12.411 --> 00:10:14.713
you sat on, and it had
a control stick

00:10:14.713 --> 00:10:16.982
that would, like, have
"brake" or "fast,"

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:18.651
and it was always broken,
so it doesn't matter.

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:21.019
You just zoom by,
and if you tried to stop,

00:10:21.019 --> 00:10:24.589
you'd scrape up your elbows
and, like -- oh, it's crazy.

00:10:24.589 --> 00:10:25.958
And they had --
-In New York?

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:27.425
-And that's the fun of the game?
Like, that's --

00:10:27.425 --> 00:10:28.994
-No, it's not supposed to be.
It's supposed to be --

00:10:28.994 --> 00:10:30.195
it's supposed to be fun.

00:10:30.195 --> 00:10:31.830
The theme park,
there's no rules.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.533
That was my first time
and last time I bungee jumped.

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:36.702
And -- and you --
cliff diving.

00:10:36.702 --> 00:10:38.970
You would jump off this cliff.

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:42.942
And you'd jump off like an
18-foot cliff into a pool,

00:10:42.942 --> 00:10:44.176
a swimming pool.

00:10:44.176 --> 00:10:45.845
And then, people would just
jump on you

00:10:45.845 --> 00:10:47.646
because there's no rules.
-That's crazy.

00:10:47.646 --> 00:10:49.281
-No, it's really crazy.

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:50.916
So it was called Action Park.

00:10:50.916 --> 00:10:52.751
I loved it.
I think I did.

00:10:52.751 --> 00:10:54.887
I don't even remember.
It was probably terrible. But --

00:10:54.887 --> 00:10:57.723
-It sounds pretty terrible.
It sounds like Action Park

00:10:57.723 --> 00:11:00.392
was about that swindle life.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.392 --> 00:11:01.927
-It might be on an
episode, man.

00:11:01.927 --> 00:11:03.495
Never know.
I got to check it out.

00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:05.130
But we're here.
We're back in the building.

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.832
I'm psyched to see
everybody here

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:08.567
and everyone for doing this.

00:11:08.567 --> 00:11:09.802
And very, very cool.

00:11:09.802 --> 00:11:11.670
Upstairs, "Late Night
With Seth Meyers"

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:13.638
